By Golok Nanmwa, Jos
A woman has been killed, while two others sustained injuries while harvesting groundnuts on a farm at Gwom-Ajang, Foron District, in Barkin Ladi Local Government Area of Plateau State.
The incident occurred at about 4pm on Saturday, according to a member of the community, Silas Bitrus, who confirmed the incident to our correspondent.
Bitrus said, &#8220;The incident occurred around 4pm while they were harvesting groundnuts on the farm.&#8221;
He added, &#8220;A woman was killed, while two others sustained injuries.&#8221;
Also confirming the incident, the National Publicity Secretary of the Berom Youth Moulders, BYM, Rwang Tengwong, condemned the attacks and urged security operatives to go after the attackers.
Also in a related development, the Coalition of Plateau State Indigenous Youth Bodies has alleged a plot by some groups to launch a counter-propaganda campaign against the Department of State Services, DSS, and other security agencies operating in the state.
In a statement made available to newsmen on Saturday and signed by Amb. Ezekiel Peter Bini, Chairman, Coalition of Indigenous Youth Nationalities, Plateau State; Dalyop Solomon Mwantiri, President, Berom Youth Moulder-Association; Amb. Miri Timnan Nyantau, President, Tarok Progressive Youths Association; and Mr Jonathan Kyesmang Yusuf, President, Mwaghavul Youths Movement, the coalition said, &#8220;Following our World Press Conference held at the Nigerian Union of Journalists Secretariat in Abuja on 21st October, 2026, the Coalition has received information of a plan to launch an aggressive counter-propaganda campaign.&#8221;
The group said, &#8220;According to reliable sources, some groups are planning to stage a World Press Conference to portray the joint operations of the Department of State Services (DSS), the Mobile Police Force, and Operation Rainbow as discriminatory against a section of the population.&#8221;
The coalition further said, &#8220;The propaganda being launched must not be accepted as truth without independent verification.&#8221;
&#8220;We challenge anyone concerned about human rights and freedom to demand evidence and allow the appropriate authorities to establish the facts.&#8221;
The group added, &#8220;We stand firmly with the DSS, Mobile Police and Operation Rainbow and other security operatives.&#8221;
&#8220;We will not be distracted by propaganda, nor shall we retreat because of terror. Plateau is our heritage and must remain safe for all law-abiding citizens.&#8221;
The post Woman killed, two injured on Plateau farm appeared first on Vanguard News.
